t blue?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "pts": 2, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "unit": "times", "units": ["times"]}, {"id": "m5u08v3Bq16", "type": "num", "prompt": "A bag has 3 red and 6 blue cubes. How many red cubes must be added so that red and blue are equally likely?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "unit": "cubes", "units": ["cubes"]}, {"id": "m5u08v3Bq17", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "In 50 picks from a bag, red came up 33 times. Which is the best conclusion?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Reasoning", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "options": [{"t": "red is impossible"}, {"t": "red is certain"}, {"t": "red is likely"}]}, {"id": "m5u08v3Bq18", "type": "num", "prompt": "A counter was picked 50 times and green came up 21 times. If you did 100 picks, about how many greens would you expect?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "unit": "greens", "units": ["greens"]}, {"id": "m5u08v3Bq19", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "A coin was flipped 100 times and gave 59 heads. Which statement is best?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Reasoning", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "options": [{"t": "the next flip must be tails"}, {"t": "heads is impossible"}, {"t": "the result is close to what we expect"}]}, {"id": "m5u08v3Bq20", "type": "num", "prompt": "A fair dice is rolled 30 times. About how many times would you expect it to show a number less than 7?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "unit": "times", "units": ["times"]}, {"id": "m5u08v3Bq21", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Explain how to predict the number of heads in 50 coin flips.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Reasoning", "pts": 2, "sec": "D · Reasoning"}, {"id": "m5u08v3Bq22", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Explain why repeating an experiment more times is better.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Rea